{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "kiro-recall: Session Context Injection",
  "description": "Fires on the first prompt of each session. Runs the Relevance Detector against the vault, injects matching notes as ambient context, and surfaces a one-line session summary.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "promptSubmit"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "kiro-recall session hook — run ONCE per session only. If you have already run this hook in this session, skip it entirely and do not repeat it.\n\nSTEP 1 — Detect workspace name\nExtract the final segment of the current workspace root path. Call this Workspace_Name.\n\nSTEP 2 — Generic name check\nIf Workspace_Name is one of: src, dev, project, app, code, workspace, repo, main, test, build, website, frontend, backend, api, server, client, lib, library, core, base — skip to SECONDARY SIGNAL.\n\nSTEP 3 — PRIMARY SIGNAL\nUse the mcp-obsidian list_directory tool on \"01-projects/\" and check for a file or subfolder whose name case-insensitively matches Workspace_Name.\n- On match: use read_note (or list_directory + read_multiple_notes) to load that project note + all notes from \"06-permanent/\". Record source as \"primary\". Go to STEP 6.\n- No match: go to SECONDARY SIGNAL.\n\nSTEP 4 — SECONDARY SIGNAL\nInspect the paths of all currently open files in the workspace. Check if any path segment matches a name in \"01-projects/\".\n- On match: load that project note + all notes from \"06-permanent/\". Record source as \"secondary\". Go to STEP 6.\n- No match: check if .kiro/steering/ contains a file with a \"project\" frontmatter field that matches a name in \"01-projects/\".\n  - On match: load that project note + all notes from \"06-permanent/\". Record source as \"secondary\". Go to STEP 6.\n  - No match: go to FALLBACK.\n\nSTEP 5 — FALLBACK\nList \"06-permanent/\" and load all markdown notes there. Record source as \"fallback\".\n- If \"06-permanent/\" is empty: check \"00-inbox/\" too. If both are empty, this is a COLD VAULT — display exactly: \"Your vault is empty — no context loaded yet. That's fine, you're just getting started. Use `/recall` during this session to capture your first note. It'll land in your inbox and kiro-recall will confirm it worked.\" Then stop.\n\nSTEP 6 — INJECT and SUMMARISE\nRead all resolved notes using read_multiple_notes (max 10 per call, batch as needed). Hold the content as ambient context for this session.\n\nThen display exactly ONE summary line in this format:\n- Primary/secondary match: \"Loaded {project name} note ({source} match) + {N} permanent notes.\"\n- Fallback: \"Loaded {N} permanent notes (fallback — no project match found).\"\n- If zero permanent notes alongside a project note, omit the count entirely.\n\nFAILURE HANDLING:\n- If vault path unreachable: display \"Couldn't reach your vault at session start — context not loaded. Check that your vault path is correct in kiro-recall settings.\" and stop.\n- If MCP server unavailable: display \"The vault MCP server isn't responding — context not loaded this session. You can still use `/recall` to capture notes once it's back up.\" and stop.\n- Never surface stack traces, file paths, or internal error details."
  }
}